# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets — never treat these as text.
#
# git's own heuristic is not reliable for this repo.  It classified
# linux-port/palettes/03-red-hot.dat and linux-port/testdata/mode1000_256x192.raw
# as *text*, because neither happens to contain a NUL byte in its first 8000.
# A text-classified blob is subject to end-of-line conversion, which is
# harmless on Linux but silently corrupts the file on a clone with
# core.autocrlf=true (or a checkout with a text=auto rule).  That would break
# the palette ramps — MD5-verified against RE Docs 06 §1.3 — and the raw
# frames and frozen ground truth that `make check` compares byte-for-byte.
#
# These are tracked for the same reason the calibration blobs and the frozen
# vendor ground truth are: small, needed to build and test, and re-extractable.
# See .gitignore and the per-directory READMEs (palettes/, testdata/, calib/).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bin     binary
*.dat     binary
*.raw     binary
*.ppm     binary

# Packet captures live in MechaniscoutPcap/, which is untracked today.  Listed
# so that tracking them later cannot go wrong.
*.pcapng  binary
